1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,698
A calendar is only useful to the people who can reach it.

2
00:00:04,698 --> 00:00:09,628
This video creates a calendar, shows how its visibility and its sharing decide

3
00:00:09,628 --> 00:00:14,500
who sees what, explains the access levels, and shows the permissions that let

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,200
people use, create and manage calendars.

5
00:00:21,806 --> 00:00:24,565
Open Calendars, then Manage Calendars.

6
00:00:24,565 --> 00:00:29,832
The list shows the calendars you can see, with a search box and a Type filter.

7
00:00:29,832 --> 00:00:32,591
Choose Add calendar and pick the type.

8
00:00:32,591 --> 00:00:35,726
Here it is a General calendar for a project.

9
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:41,216
Give the calendar a Name and a Description, and choose the Color its

10
00:00:41,216 --> 00:00:42,676
events are drawn in.

11
00:00:42,676 --> 00:00:46,213
The Time zone is the one new events of this calendar use.

12
00:00:46,213 --> 00:00:49,470
Leave it on the site's time zone to follow the site.

13
00:00:49,943 --> 00:00:55,899
Visibility decides who sees the calendar besides its owner and the people it is shared with.

14
00:00:55,899 --> 00:00:58,208
Private shows it to nobody else.

15
00:00:58,208 --> 00:01:02,340
Shared lets everyone see when it is busy, but not the details.

16
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:04,893
Public lets everyone see its events.

17
00:01:04,893 --> 00:01:08,113
Enabled keeps the calendar open for new events.

18
00:01:08,564 --> 00:01:14,602
The Sharing section shares the calendar with users and roles, each at one of four levels.

19
00:01:14,602 --> 00:01:19,369
See free/busy time shows when the calendar is busy, and nothing else.

20
00:01:19,369 --> 00:01:22,484
Here the Support Team role gets that level.

21
00:01:22,935 --> 00:01:26,235
See events adds the events and their details.

22
00:01:26,235 --> 00:01:28,047
Jamie gets that level.

23
00:01:28,047 --> 00:01:33,806
Add and change events lets people add, change and cancel events, and Maria gets it.

24
00:01:33,806 --> 00:01:39,305
Manage, the highest level, also changes the calendar and who it is shared with.

25
00:01:39,768 --> 00:01:42,600
Each level includes the ones before it.

26
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:48,328
The person who creates a calendar, and the calendar administrators, always manage it.

27
00:01:48,328 --> 00:01:53,868
Under Overlaps, Limit overlapping events refuses a busy event when the calendar is

28
00:01:53,868 --> 00:01:56,764
already full, which is how a room works.

29
00:01:56,764 --> 00:01:59,344
A project calendar doesn't need it.

30
00:01:59,344 --> 00:02:00,478
Choose Save.

31
00:02:04,646 --> 00:02:06,641
Jamie was given See events.

32
00:02:06,641 --> 00:02:12,080
Project Falcon is listed with his other calendars, and its events show their titles.

33
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:16,553
Clicking one opens its details, but there is no Edit, because he can

34
00:02:16,553 --> 00:02:18,306
only read the calendar.

35
00:02:19,896 --> 00:02:24,587
Alex belongs to the Support Team, which was given See free/busy time.

36
00:02:24,587 --> 00:02:28,902
The calendar is listed for him too, but its events show only as

37
00:02:28,902 --> 00:02:31,779
Busy, with their times and nothing else.

38
00:02:31,779 --> 00:02:36,406
Anyone who can't open an event sees it this way wherever it appears.

39
00:02:40,608 --> 00:02:45,039
Calendar permissions are on the role page, under Access Control, Roles.

40
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:50,103
Use calendars lets someone have a personal calendar and reach the calendars shared

41
00:02:50,103 --> 00:02:53,211
with them, and everyone who is signed in has it.

42
00:02:53,211 --> 00:02:57,988
Create calendars lets someone create calendars, and the creator manages them.

43
00:02:58,438 --> 00:03:03,701
View all calendars gives read access to every calendar, and Manage all calendars

44
00:03:03,701 --> 00:03:05,966
gives full access to every one.

45
00:03:05,966 --> 00:03:08,658
Give these two to administrators only.

46
00:03:09,109 --> 00:03:14,868
List anyone's calendar events lets someone see anyone's schedule, and View anyone's calendar

47
00:03:14,868 --> 00:03:19,746
events lets them open the events of any calendar instead of seeing busy time.

48
00:03:19,746 --> 00:03:24,389
The own versions, for a person's own schedule and the events they created

49
00:03:24,389 --> 00:03:26,799
or attend, come with Use calendars.

50
00:03:28,799 --> 00:03:33,423
Create the calendar, choose its visibility, share it at the level each person

51
00:03:33,423 --> 00:03:36,710
needs, and give roles only the permissions they need.

52
00:03:36,710 --> 00:03:38,159
Thanks for watching.

